iew analyzes the available structural data and proposes a consensus interpretation that facilitates an understanding of the pathological problems derived from impairment of MAT function.\nL38: In addition, new research opportunities directed toward clarification of aspects that remain obscure are also identified.\nL39: This is a preview of subscription content, to check access.\nL40: ## Access this article\nL41: \nL42: Log in via an institution\nL43: \nL44: ## Subscribe and save\nL45: \nL46: Springer+\nL47: \nL48: from $39.99 /Month\nL49: \nL50:   * Starting from 10 chapters or articles per month\nL51:   * Access and download chapters and articles from more than 300k books and 2,500 journals\nL52:   * Cancel anytime\nL53: 【17†View plans】\nL54: ## Buy Now\nL55: \nL56: [Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input]\nL57: \nL58: Buy article PDF USD 39.95\nL59: \nL60: Price excludes VAT (USA)\nL61: Tax calculation will be finalised during checkout.\nL62: \nL63: Instant access to the full article PDF.\nL64: \nL65: 【18†Institutional subscriptions†www.springernature.com】\nL66: \nL67: ### Similar content being viewed by others\nL68: \nL69: 【19†Image†media.springernature.com】\nL70: ### 【20†Structural insights into DNA N^{6}-adenine methylation by the MTA1 complex】\nL71: \nL72: Article Open access 20 January 2023\nL73: \nL74: 【21†Image†media.springernature.com】\nL75: \nL76: ### 【22†Engineering of Methionine Adenosyltransferase Reveals Key Roles of Electrostatic Interactions in Enhanced Catalytic Activity】\nL77: \nL78: Article 29 August 2023\nL79: \nL80: 【23†Image†media.springernature.com】\nL81: \nL82: ### 【24†Analogs of S-Adenosyl-L-Methionine in Studies of Methyltransferases】\nL83: \nL84: Article 14 April 2022\nL85: \nL86: ## Author information\nL87: ### Authors and Affiliations\nL88: \nL89:   1. Institute for Cancer Research, Fox Chase Cancer Center, 333 Cottman Avenue, Philadelphia, PA, 19111, USA\nL90: \nL91: G. D. Markham\nL92: \nL93:   2. Instituto de I